# NAMED-INDIVIDUAL DECLARATIONS ARE OPTIONAL. :stewie is asserted into two
# disjoint classes and declared as nothing, so the ontology is INCONSISTENT.
# A context registry keyed on declarations never creates individual(stewie):
# its class assertions then derive nothing, coverage still reads complete, and
# the verdict is a FALSE COHERENT. Found by the W3C OWL 2 conformance test
# DisjointClasses-002 (corpus/conformance.py); this is its shape.
# Expect: INCOHERENT (inconsistent), exit 1.

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:Boy a owl:Class ; owl:disjointWith :Girl .
:Girl a owl:Class .
:stewie a :Boy , :Girl .
